(Comparative Efficacy of Single-Modality Versus Multimodal Neuroimaging for Brain-Machine) Tj
T*
(Interface Rehabilitation Systems: Protocol for a Controlled Training Study) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Brain-computer interfaces coupled with muscle stimulation represent promising adjuncts to) Tj
T*
(post-stroke recovery protocols. However, uncertainty remains regarding optimal signal) Tj
T*
(acquisition strategies. This protocol describes a blinded comparative trial investigating) Tj
T*
(whether combined electroencephalographic and optical neuroimaging provides advantages over) Tj
T*
(electroencephalography alone in supporting motor control via electrical muscle) Tj
T*
(stimulation. Objectives: To compare classification performance, user experience, and) Tj
T*
(physiological measures across single-modality and dual-modality signal processing) Tj
T*
(pipelines. Methods: Healthy volunteer participants will undergo identical training) Tj
T*
(regimens with either combined or single-modality signal interfaces over a three-day) Tj
T*
(period. Outcome measurement focuses on real-time classification accuracy, subjective) Tj
T*
(agency ratings, attentional load assessment, and comfort metrics. We hypothesize that) Tj
T*
(multimodal acquisition will yield superior performance; secondary objectives include) Tj
T*
(channel optimization and feasibility assessment.) Tj
